#
# The SIGCHLD trap runs once per reaped child. run_pending_traps used to run
# the queued firings once and then continue to the next signal, so a child
# reaped while the trap was executing queued a firing that nothing in that
# pass came back for -- and at end of input nothing ever parsed again to
# collect it. Statistical control, not proof: the loss was intermittent
# (about one round in five here), so thirty clean rounds carry it past a
# hundred to one. Only the losing-round count is printed, so timing never
# reaches the expected output.

losses=0
for i in {1..30}; do
	n=$(${THIS_SH} ./trapchld.sub 2>&1 | grep -c CHLD)
	[ "$n" -eq 11 ] || losses=$((losses + 1))
done
echo "rounds with lost SIGCHLD trap firings: $losses"

# The other dispatch path lost firings by a different mechanism. waitchld runs
# the SIGCHLD trap directly when the wait builtin reaps a child, and that call
# never marks SIGCHLD in progress, so a run_pending_traps entered from inside
# that trap matched none of the three SIGCHLD branches and fell through to the
# bad-handler branch, which warns and then discards the queued firings.
#
# What is asserted here is that branch never being taken, which is exactly what
# the fix guarantees and is decisive: measured on this tree without the fix,
# the probe below trips it in 14 of 2000 rounds, so a thousand rounds expect
# seven. Run serially on purpose -- parallel load suppresses the window rather
# than widening it.
#
# The firing count is deliberately NOT asserted over this probe. A third,
# undiagnosed loss remains (a reap accounted by waitchld that is neither queued
# nor run: no warning, nothing left pending at exit) at roughly one round in a
# thousand under load. Asserting the count here would make the suite
# intermittently red for a bug that is not fixed yet, which is worse than the
# bug. It is recorded in PLAN.md and in BUGFIX_REPRO_REPORTS with its counter
# evidence; promote the count assertion here once it is closed.
warned=0
for i in {1..1000}; do
	case $(${THIS_SH} ./trapchld2.sub 2>&1) in
	*"bad value in trap_list"*) warned=$((warned + 1)) ;;
	esac
done
echo "self-spawn rounds discarding a queued firing: $warned"
